course: dictionary
lesson: 9514
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Sticky is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «Many frogs catch insects with a long, sticky tongue.» The frog catches insects with its tongue, so sticky means able to hold on to things.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? Then try a meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense. A sticky tongue catches insects, so "able to hold on" works. A sticky tongue is not hot or damp, so that meaning does not fit.
explain: Sticky can also describe the weather or a problem. On a hot, damp day the air feels heavy and you may get sweaty. A sticky situation is not about glue at all. It is a problem that is hard or awkward to get out of.
fact: Sticky means covered with something like glue, honey or syrup that sticks to things.
fact: Sticky can mean able to stick to surfaces, like sticky tape or a sticky note.
fact: Sticky weather is hot and damp, and it can make you feel sweaty.
fact: A sticky situation is difficult or awkward to get out of.
fact: «Many frogs catch insects with a long, sticky tongue.» Here sticky means able to hold on to things.
exercise: «Many frogs catch insects with a long, sticky tongue.» What does sticky mean here? | Hot and damp | *Able to hold on to things | Covered in honey, very messy | Difficult to get out of
exercise: Mum says, «The kitchen floor is sticky, so please mop it up.» What does sticky mean? | Able to stick a note to the fridge | Hot and damp weather | A hard situation to escape | *Covered with something that sticks, like syrup
exercise: Dad says, «We are in a sticky situation with the car.» What does sticky mean? | *Difficult or awkward | Able to stick to the wall | Hot and damp | Covered in glue
test: The weather is hot, damp and muggy, so Ruby says it is sticky. What does sticky mean? | Able to stick to surfaces | *Hot and damp, making you feel sweaty | Covered with glue | Difficult to get out of
test: «A sticky note on the screen can be read by anyone passing.» What does sticky mean in this sentence? | *Able to stick to surfaces | Hot and damp | A hard problem | Covered with honey
exam: Which sentence uses sticky to mean hot and damp? | *«The sticky air made the walk feel long.» | «The sticky tape held the poster up.» | «He was in a sticky spot with his homework.» | «Her hands were sticky with jam.»
